- !!!We use pnpm as our package manager, as well as pnpm workspaces to help manage our monorepo packages
    - We use turbo repo to help manage and optimize our monorepo
        - ALWAYS remove unnecessary comments when refactoring
            - ALWAYS remove unused imports when refactoring or finishing a task

Use Path Aliases Wherever possible:

```json
'@components': require.resolve('./src/components'),
'@shared-components': require.resolve('./src/shared-components'),
'@utils': require.resolve('./src/utils'),
'@styles': require.resolve('./src/styles'),
'@types': require.resolve('./src/types'),
'@store': require.resolve('./src/store'),
'@providers': require.resolve('./src/providers'),
'@data': require.resolve('./src/data'),
'@pages': require.resolve('./src/pages'),
'@contexts': require.resolve('./src/contexts'),
'@analytics': require.resolve('./src/analytics'),
```

Mantine Theme Color Access Pattern — Summary for Refactor

1. Correct Access Pattern
Always use Mantine's color palette arrays:
Apply to typescript - e...
theme.colors[theme.primaryColor][6] // for primary color (main shade)
theme.colors.blue[6]                // for blue palette, main shade
theme.colors.cyan[6]                // for cyan palette, main shade
theme.colors.dark[8]                // for dark backgrounds
theme.white                         // for white
theme.black    
For gradients or custom colors:
Use theme.other.heroGradient, theme.other.accentGradient, etc., as defined in your custom theme.
For text and backgrounds:
Text: theme.colors.gray[7], theme.colors.dark[0], or theme.colors[theme.primaryColor][7]
Background: theme.colors.dark[8], theme.colors.gray[0], etc.
For border radius, spacing, and shadows:
theme.radius.md
theme.spacing.lg
theme.shadows.md

2. TypeScript Pattern
If using styled-components with Mantine theme, always cast theme:
Apply to typescript - e...
}

3. Examples from Your Codebase
theme.colors[theme.primaryColor][6] — for main brand color
theme.colors.dark[8] — for dark backgrounds
theme.colors.gray[6] — for neutral text
theme.colors.blue[6] — for blue accent
theme.colors.cyan[6] — for cyan accent
theme.shadows.md — for box shadows
theme.radius.md — for border radius